git -C $csrbt commit -m "ADR-148: the lab bench, entered whole -- and the two entry paths agree" `
  -m "The third page taken whole. ecology-lab.html was ADR-144's third-largest gap at 7 of 40 fields, and the seven were the seeded terrarium and four defaults: the workbench underneath -- diversity, beta diversity, mark-recapture, quadrat dispersion, Hardy-Weinberg, a Punnett builder with a chi-square fit, a dichotomous key, Newick trees, a seeded flashcard drill, six theory models and an .eco round trip -- was entered by nothing, and every one of those is a published formula the page computes itself. The task goes 22 steps to 129: 7 -> 40 OF 40 FIELDS, 74 -> 202 confirmed expectations, and the kit 279 -> 312 of 518, 54% -> 60%. THE TWO ENTRY PATHS AGREE. Every count box on this page has a CHIP ADDER over it -- a name field, a count field, an Add button and plus/minus chips per species -- because that is the entry a gloved thumb on a wet tablet can actually hit. It writes through to the textarea underneath and the textarea writes back to the chips, and nothing had ever pressed it. One claim now holds both halves: adding heron 5 through the chip adder writes 'heron 5' into the textarea AND moves the figures to six species, H' 1.33, J' 0.75, Chao1 6, and typing the old list straight back into the textarea returns them to five, 1.16 and 5. Site A gains lily through its chips, site B gains moss through its own, and site A is retyped as text. Every figure is RECOMPUTED by a Python port of the page's own arithmetic: the terrarium at J' 0.73, 29.2 effective species and Chao1 100, 0.43 at a 95% hot share, 0.88 at a hot set of 20, the island 616/604 at capacity 12 and 342/310 at 32; Jaccard 0.5, Sorensen 0.67, Bray-Curtis 0.31 sharing 3 of 6 kinds, 0.67/0.8/0.25 with lily, and 1/1/0 when the two sites are made identical; Lincoln-Petersen 360, Chapman 354 and a 95% CI of 268-440, with Chapman still at 11,010 when R = 0 leaves Lincoln-Petersen undefined; variance/mean 26.12 and Morisita 3.51 (clumped), 0 and 0.82 for eight equal quadrats; p 0.543, q 0.458, chi-square 0.22 and expected 294/496/209, 8.19 and out of equilibrium for 400/489/213, exactly 0 for 250/500/250; 3 R_ : 1 rr with Mendel's 5474/1850 at chi-square 0.263 against critical 3.841, 1 : 2 : 1 under incomplete dominance, the dihybrid at 9 : 3 : 3 : 1 with 315/108/101/32 at 0.47 against 7.815; three couplets walked yes-no-yes to butterfly or moth with the trail kept; seven taxa at depth 6; and a five-card drill dealing detritivore first at seed 7 and decomposer at seed 0. THREE THINGS THIS FOUND. (1) THE ORACLE'S FORMATTER WAS WRONG, AND QUIETLY. The page prints through Number(x).toLocaleString('en-US', {maximumFractionDigits: d}), which rounds HALF AWAY FROM ZERO and does so on the SHORTEST ROUND-TRIP DECIMAL of the double rather than on the double itself. Python's round() is half-to-even on the binary value and disagreed on both counts: Hardy-Weinberg's p came out 0.542 against a page showing 0.543, and 2.675 rounds to 2.68 on the page and 2.67 in Python. The port is Decimal(repr(x)) with ROUND_HALF_UP. A formatter that is wrong on ties is wrong on roughly one figure in a thousand, which is exactly often enough to be dismissed as a rounding quibble and never fixed. (2) AN OCCURRENCE INDEX IS NOT AN ADDRESS. read-report distinguishes repeated figure labels with '#2', and this page prints 'evenness J-prime' three times, so writing output.figures.evenness #2 made the task depend on how many tiles happen to sit above it -- which is ADR-145's lesson about unnamed controls, one layer up. The task addresses figures by the box that owns them instead: output.by.wb-field-out.evenness. (3) SEED 0 IS A SEED. The page's own comment records that ``+value || 42`` once sent seed 0 silently back to the default deck order, 'a perfectly ordinary thing for a student to ask for', and the fix had never been held. It is now, by the mulberry32 port running the same Fisher-Yates. NINE REFUSALS are entered on purpose and each held to the sentence the page prints: R above min(M, C); two quadrats minimum; a key line without its two pipes; a key that points at itself (this key loops); an unbalanced Newick string; a drill with no cards; K = 0; K1 = 0; a negative distance; negative steps. And the .eco import is held to LOADING rather than reporting -- the field counts become the imported pond's three species, so an importer that said 'imported' and changed nothing would not pass. The terrarium's three slider readouts -- o-hot, o-set, o-cap -- were figures no task could read (ADR-146); renamed to o-hotOut, o-setOut and o-capOut and held, so ecology-lab is the second page in the kit with ZERO blind figures and the kit reads 233 of 256 written elements readable, 23 blind on 8 pages. verify_eco 138, unchanged in count. Held: a Python port catches a change in the page but not a shared misunderstanding of the method, and ADR-133's binding of the shipped protocol to the Java science engine is the check that covers that, unchanged here; releve at 7 of 42 and experiment-guide at 16 of 52 are the largest gaps left; and the chip adder's plus/minus and delete buttons are pressed by no task yet, since they are controls rather than fields and entry_reach reads 40 of 40 with them untouched. TWO THINGS THE ENTRY BROKE, AND BOTH WERE THE INSTRUMENT. (a) A CONTROL THE ENTRY LEFT FOCUSED could not be asked what focus looks like: the chip adder returns focus to its count box after Add, so the entered lab ended with 'site B count' focused, and audit_focus then reported 'no visible focus' on a page whose ring is fine -- because the unfocused reading it compared against was taken while the control was focused. Nothing on the page was wrong; the instrument could not ask the question. The probe now blurs each control before reading its resting state, switches transitions off for the length of the probe (a ring mid-transition answers with a value from a hundred milliseconds ago, which is ADR-131's lesson one layer down), and PUTS FOCUS BACK where the page had it, because the audits run one after another on the same tab and a probe that leaves focus moved changes what the next one measures. verify_audit_states 70, mutate_audit_states 47/47. (b) A CHECK WAS ASSERTING SOMETHING OTHER THAN WHAT IT SAID: verify_tasks compared the tasks that entered with no destructive rung against THE TASKS THAT DECLARE A POLICY AT ALL, which was the same set only for as long as every policy in the kit went all the way to DESTRUCTIVE. This task is the first to declare one that stops short -- it opens SENSITIVE_READ, DRAFT and MUTATE and says why it needs no more -- and the arithmetic then counted it on both sides. The sentence the check prints always said 'the tasks that did NOT declare IT'; the set it used did not. verify_tasks 285. Both faults appeared only because the entry got further than it used to, which is the coupling entry_reach and audit_readable already have, cutting the useful way: every page taken whole is an audit taken further." `
  -m "Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>" -m "Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CNn3hvazSDBU2TCgsGXjTt"
